WEBVTT

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:09.170
Waking up early sure is hard.

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:11.960
Morning, Tsuda-kun.

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:13.550
Good morning.

00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:16.760
Are you going to have breakfast now?

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:18.550
Yeah, I was running short on time.

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:21.520
Will pan bread and tea be enough?

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:23.140
Well, I'm also running short on money.

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:26.810
Tsuda, what's this I'm hearing from Aria?

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:29.730
You didn't start the day very healthily.

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:32.110
Pan... tea for breakfast?

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:33.690
What are you on about?

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:39.700
Ousai Academy Student Council Rules:

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:42.580
article two, clause nine!

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:45.290
Eat cucumbers with your mouth whenever possible!

00:00:45.290 --> 00:00:47.000
Not "whenever possible"! Always!

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:56.840
Looks like Hata has something on her mind.

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:58.510
You can tell?

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:01.260
Womens' intuition is always on the mark!

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:05.390
I once randomly filled in
my answer sheet just for fun.

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:07.180
In the end, I scored forty-two percent!

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:09.640
I'm not sure what to make of that accuracy rate.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:15.440
She noticed us.

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:16.480
We should go.

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:18.440
So you saw.

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:21.280
The thing is...

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:26.490
All of the other club members are absent due to personal reasons,

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:29.910
and I can't get this issue out by myself, so I was thinking of suspending it.

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:32.160
Why so distant?

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:35.170
We're here for you!

00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:37.290
Exactly.

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:38.170
Boing!

00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:39.630
That's too bouncy!

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:41.170
Jeez, I hate that about you!

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:44.300
We don't have any second-year members.

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:47.760
This is what happens the moment the first-years are unavailable.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:51.480
And here I thought you were
putting out the newspapers by yourself.

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:52.940
Me too.

00:03:53.270 --> 00:03:55.060
There's not much time left.

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:57.310
Could you please start right away?

00:03:57.310 --> 00:03:57.940
Sure.

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:00.110
First, let's take care of the school survey.

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:02.610
This issue's survey is "things that are hard to say."

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:04.200
What do you mean by that?

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:09.990
We ask people for phrases they think are
difficult to pronounce and rank them by frequency.

00:04:09.990 --> 00:04:11.700
I see.

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:13.960
Let's start with the teachers.

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:15.620
Um...

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:18.670
Hohenzollern-Sigmaringen.

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:19.960
What the heck is that?

00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:23.300
Zarathustra?

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:25.970
Guess they'd pull one from their own subject.

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:31.140
The sixth sick sheik's shixth sheep's shick.

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:33.600
That does sound hard to say...

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:34.100
Takatoshi's Body

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:34.390
Are there any words that you find hard to say, Ms. Yokoshima?
Takatoshi's Body

00:04:34.390 --> 00:04:38.360
Are there any words that you find hard to say, Ms. Yokoshima?

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:42.280
"We should break up."

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:44.490
I asked the wrong person.

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:48.570
I think the word "befuddling" is kind of befuddling.

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:52.540
Oh, I'm talking about words that are hard to say.

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:55.040
Sometimes, I'm not sure what order the letters go.

00:04:57.210 --> 00:05:00.460
I guess there are times when you switch letters around by mistake.

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:02.500
You've mixed up something too, Shichijou-senpai?

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:04.260
Scat!

00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:06.380
How do you even get <i>that</i> wrong?

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:12.890
Prez, would you mind transcribing this interview for me?

00:05:12.890 --> 00:05:14.520
Sure, I can give it a shot.

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:17.940
It's my own interview!

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:19.270
This feels kinda weird.

00:05:22.110 --> 00:05:24.940
Now that I'm hearing myself, I was kinda boring.

00:05:24.940 --> 00:05:26.780
Maybe I should make it more—

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:28.110
Hata...

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:28.820
Yes?

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:31.580
I think I understand your
approach to journalism now.

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:37.370
Hata, what's that?

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:40.580
The photo I'm using for your interview.

00:05:41.670 --> 00:05:42.670
Don't do that!

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:46.130
I said a <i>ten</i> percent increase!

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:48.010
This makes it way too obvious!

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:49.180
She told her to do it?

00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:52.260
This looks like ten percent to me.

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:54.140
Oh, really?

00:05:54.140 --> 00:05:55.930
And <i>she</i> talked her into agreeing.

00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:59.690
Next, we have this issue's main headline.

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:00.480
We have a tip that the P.E. teacher, Mr. Daimon,
and the music teacher, Ms. Michishita, are now engaged.

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:01.730
I'm Mr. Daimon.

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:02.980
I'm Ms. Michishita.

00:06:02.980 --> 00:06:06.610
We have a tip that the P.E. teacher, Mr. Daimon,
and the music teacher, Ms. Michishita, are now engaged.

00:06:06.610 --> 00:06:07.820
R-Really?!

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:16.450
Oh, they might be.

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:19.540
I knew it! Something happened during the trip to Okinawa!

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:19.790
I'm sorry I didn't tell you!
I knew it! Something happened during the trip to Okinawa!

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:21.540
Right? <i>Right</i>?
I'm sorry I didn't tell you!

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:22.670
Please don't eat me! Please!
Right? <i>Right</i>?

00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:23.460
Please don't eat me! Please!

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:27.210
Anyway, at the moment, it's only a tip.

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:28.840
I'd like confirmation.

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:31.220
But would they tell us if we asked?

00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:34.220
Leave it to my brilliant conversational skills.

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:35.970
They'll spill everything if I just bait it out!

00:06:35.970 --> 00:06:37.930
What do you think, Prez?

00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:41.730
Can't say I'm not curious.

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:45.440
If it's true, it'd be great news.

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:47.480
I think it's a good thing.

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:48.490
Yeah, you're right.

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:51.910
Plus, I believe one's body <i>and</i> intentions should always be exposed!

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:54.620
Okay, please do <i>not</i> expose your body!

00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:56.700
All right!

00:06:56.700 --> 00:06:58.250
Commence operation!

00:06:58.660 --> 00:07:00.250
We'd like to borrow her for a minute.

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:02.040
O-Okay...

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:04.710
Hold on, you two. Where are you taking me?

00:07:04.710 --> 00:07:06.380
No need to worry.

00:07:07.130 --> 00:07:08.630
What do you want?

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:10.590
Oh, um... Could you spare a minute?

00:07:18.930 --> 00:07:20.180
Hello.

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:21.980
I'm with the Newspaper Club.

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:24.270
Oh, if it isn't Hata!

00:07:24.650 --> 00:07:28.440
You seem to be quite close to each other.

00:07:29.570 --> 00:07:33.410
We've heard a few rumors about the two of you,

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:36.450
which is why you were promptly summoned here.

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:39.410
I admit nothing.

00:07:39.410 --> 00:07:42.040
Teachers have their own private lives.

00:07:42.040 --> 00:07:44.370
Oh, I see.

00:07:44.370 --> 00:07:45.790
That's quite unfortunate.

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:49.550
But I saw.

00:07:50.510 --> 00:07:52.300
The two of you.

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:55.050
As you stuck it in!

00:07:55.050 --> 00:07:56.550
She means the ring.

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:00.140
Why not?

00:08:00.770 --> 00:08:03.810
I am engaged to Mr. Daimon.

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:08.150
My sincere congratulations!

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:09.780
Th-Thank you...

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:12.650
Come on, guys! Snap 'em, snap 'em.

00:08:12.650 --> 00:08:13.860
Congratulations!

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:15.320
Th-Thank you...
Congratulations!

00:08:22.700 --> 00:08:25.080
She beat me to it!

00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:28.250
Congratulations!

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:31.090
Must be nice having a young wife!

00:08:31.090 --> 00:08:32.590
Get to your laps!

00:08:33.090 --> 00:08:36.090
Congratulations on your
engagement, Ms. Michishita!

00:08:36.090 --> 00:08:38.680
This is much too early.

00:08:38.680 --> 00:08:40.640
They're a sign of our good wishes!

00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:42.100
Please accept them!

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:44.980
Thank you.

00:08:45.390 --> 00:08:48.360
We were able to get the issue out thanks to you.

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:51.020
Please allow me to repay you somehow.

00:08:51.020 --> 00:08:52.730
There's no need for that.

00:08:52.730 --> 00:08:55.860
No, that wouldn't feel right to me.

00:08:56.280 --> 00:08:59.240
Then let's say you owe us one.

00:08:59.830 --> 00:09:01.240
Blow you one?

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:02.740
You want me to suck it?

00:09:02.740 --> 00:09:04.750
Can't end on a good note, can we?

00:09:12.420 --> 00:09:13.460
Who's that?

00:09:13.460 --> 00:09:14.510
Beats me.

00:09:15.470 --> 00:09:16.760
Hey, you two...

00:09:17.380 --> 00:09:19.260
Why aren't you going in?

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:22.680
Well, there's a woman we don't know
on the President's chair...

00:09:22.970 --> 00:09:25.270
But Tsuda-kun's right here.

00:09:25.270 --> 00:09:26.180
Whoa!

00:09:26.180 --> 00:09:27.440
When did I become a chair?

00:09:27.850 --> 00:09:29.400
Long time no see!

00:09:31.060 --> 00:09:33.530
F-Furuya-senpai?!

00:09:33.530 --> 00:09:36.490
It's the previous Ousai Academy Student Council President!

00:09:36.490 --> 00:09:38.070
Nice to meet you!

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:46.000
Why the sudden visit?

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:49.580
I came to see a few of my old teachers,
and I felt like stopping by.

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:53.050
You've changed quite a bit.

00:09:53.050 --> 00:09:55.550
Of course! I'm a gorgeous university student now.

00:09:55.550 --> 00:09:57.300
Gotta look bodacious!

00:09:57.300 --> 00:09:58.090
"Bodacious"?

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:00.760
In other words, you've lost your virginity?

00:10:00.760 --> 00:10:04.220
Did you really have to be so direct?

00:10:04.220 --> 00:10:07.060
You haven't changed a bit, Amakusa.

00:10:07.060 --> 00:10:08.730
Really?

00:10:08.730 --> 00:10:11.900
Do you still like dirty talk?

00:10:11.900 --> 00:10:12.980
I do!

00:10:12.980 --> 00:10:14.650
That's great!

00:10:14.650 --> 00:10:18.610
Actual conversation aside, it feels weird
seeing the Prez acting like a junior to anyone.

00:10:18.610 --> 00:10:19.490
Yeah.

00:10:19.490 --> 00:10:22.490
You haven't changed a bit either, Shichijou.

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:23.990
Really?

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:26.700
Still not wearing anything underneath?

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:28.870
Not wearing anything, but keeping one in!

00:10:28.870 --> 00:10:30.170
That's great!

00:10:30.170 --> 00:10:31.920
She's been this way forever, huh?

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:34.500
And Furuya-san's got nerves of steel.

00:10:35.050 --> 00:10:37.170
And who might you two be?

00:10:37.170 --> 00:10:39.260
I'm Tsuda, the vice-president.

00:10:39.260 --> 00:10:41.340
I'm Hagimura, the treasurer.

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:43.640
You seem very capable.

00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:45.140
Pleased to meet you.

00:10:45.640 --> 00:10:49.060
She didn't say anything about my height!

00:10:49.060 --> 00:10:50.770
I think I like her!

00:10:51.310 --> 00:10:53.770
Oh, were you doing the accounting?

00:10:54.230 --> 00:10:56.150
Let me help you with that.

00:10:56.150 --> 00:10:57.610
I'm good with math.

00:10:57.610 --> 00:10:59.530
Thank you very much.

00:10:59.530 --> 00:11:01.280
I'll go get a calculator.

00:11:01.280 --> 00:11:03.160
Don't worry!

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:04.990
I've got an abacus with me!

00:11:04.990 --> 00:11:05.870
Huh?

00:11:05.870 --> 00:11:07.790
I'm bad with those newfangled computer-thingies.

00:11:08.330 --> 00:11:11.330
I brought your favorites: karinto and kelp tea.

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:12.870
Thanks!

00:11:12.870 --> 00:11:14.210
Traditional.

00:11:14.210 --> 00:11:15.290
An old girl.

00:11:20.050 --> 00:11:21.680
A whoopee cushion?

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:23.550
Oh, sorry.

00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:25.510
That's your seat now?

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:27.680
I wanted to get Amakusa with that one.

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:29.930
Even her jokes are old-fashioned.

00:11:29.930 --> 00:11:31.390
Who was that?

00:11:31.390 --> 00:11:33.190
Who let out that massive queef?

00:11:33.190 --> 00:11:35.940
You haven't changed a bit either, Ms. Yokoshima.

00:11:37.150 --> 00:11:38.570
Is that you, Furuya?

00:11:38.570 --> 00:11:39.940
Long time no see!

00:11:40.360 --> 00:11:43.200
Wow, you've changed a lot.

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:44.200
Not at all.

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:48.330
You look young as ever.

00:11:48.330 --> 00:11:48.950
Well, yeah.

00:11:49.540 --> 00:11:53.170
You must be devouring boys left and right
now that the school's co-ed.

00:11:53.170 --> 00:11:54.830
Whatever could you be talking about?

00:12:01.670 --> 00:12:02.840
Is something the matter?

00:12:03.260 --> 00:12:04.380
Oh no, nothing.

00:12:04.380 --> 00:12:07.050
You're the first male student council member we've ever had.

00:12:07.050 --> 00:12:09.510
I was just thinking about how you had a soy face.

00:12:09.510 --> 00:12:10.720
"Soy face"?

00:12:11.350 --> 00:12:14.810
An Japanese term from the 80s to describe the male face.

00:12:14.810 --> 00:12:19.230
A "soy face" looked Japanese, while a "sauce face" looked European, was it?

00:12:19.610 --> 00:12:22.400
Then a "ketchup face" would look like
a shounen manga character?

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:24.740
The term existed, but it didn't mean that.

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:27.240
I just realized!

00:12:27.780 --> 00:12:29.490
Amakusa's using a computer!

00:12:29.490 --> 00:12:30.580
Took you long enough!

00:12:31.500 --> 00:12:33.250
I've been making progress too.

00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:35.710
Ooh, those are some big words!

00:12:35.710 --> 00:12:37.000
Bet you're just putting on airs.

00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:39.630
I wouldn't be so sure if I were you!

00:12:39.630 --> 00:12:40.250
What?

00:12:40.250 --> 00:12:40.840
star

00:12:40.840 --> 00:12:42.880
If you type "star" like this and hit space,
star

00:12:43.300 --> 00:12:45.180
it actually turns into a star!

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:46.010
Whoa!

00:12:46.680 --> 00:12:49.550
When did <i>you</i> become a PC master?

00:12:49.550 --> 00:12:51.140
I was the one who taught her that, though.

00:12:51.810 --> 00:12:53.480
And if you do this...

00:12:53.480 --> 00:12:53.890
Huh?

00:12:54.390 --> 00:12:58.060
Tsuda! I typed out "lewd shower stool," but it didn't turn into the mark!

00:12:58.060 --> 00:12:59.900
What? You actually thought it would?

00:13:00.650 --> 00:13:03.780
Sorry you had to walk me all the way here.

00:13:03.780 --> 00:13:05.530
Don't be. We don't see you very often.

00:13:05.530 --> 00:13:07.160
Please drop by again.

00:13:07.610 --> 00:13:09.410
Oh, right.

00:13:09.410 --> 00:13:12.660
Lemme give you something nice before I leave.

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:14.660
People still do that?

00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:19.290
We're having a university fair soon,
so feel free to stop by.

00:13:19.290 --> 00:13:20.540
Thank you.

00:13:21.630 --> 00:13:23.050
See you later.

00:13:23.050 --> 00:13:25.010
Byewell!

00:13:25.010 --> 00:13:26.010
"Byewell"?!

00:13:26.010 --> 00:13:26.840
That's old!

00:13:26.840 --> 00:13:28.470
That was some classic fanservice.

00:13:28.470 --> 00:13:29.890
Take care!

00:13:29.890 --> 00:13:31.810
The tickets are all scrunched up.

00:13:38.900 --> 00:13:41.520
This is the first time I've been to a university.

00:13:41.520 --> 00:13:42.770
Me too.

00:13:43.400 --> 00:13:45.990
It should be mine too, but...

00:13:46.900 --> 00:13:51.280
I could swear I've seen this place before.

00:13:51.280 --> 00:13:52.030
Huh?

00:13:52.700 --> 00:13:53.700
Oh, I remember!

00:13:54.290 --> 00:13:58.120
It was the backdrop for this
amateur porn photo in a magazine.

00:13:58.750 --> 00:14:01.040
There was this girl right up
against this pillar and she...

00:14:01.040 --> 00:14:03.460
After all that build-up,
<i>this</i> is the punchline we get?!

00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:05.710
Oh, you're here.

00:14:05.710 --> 00:14:06.920
Ciao!

00:14:06.920 --> 00:14:07.720
Hello.

00:14:08.590 --> 00:14:10.970
Your dress is gorgeous!

00:14:10.970 --> 00:14:13.010
It's a Western-style costume.

00:14:13.010 --> 00:14:16.390
Our fair's theme is cross-cultural exchange, after all.

00:14:16.390 --> 00:14:19.140
We should do this at our school too.

00:14:19.140 --> 00:14:19.980
Yeah.

00:14:19.980 --> 00:14:22.230
We could all make clothes. It'd be so much fun.

00:14:22.770 --> 00:14:25.070
We could have some kinky fun measuring people up, too.

00:14:25.070 --> 00:14:27.570
The measurements of the girl you like will be laid bare for you to see!

00:14:27.570 --> 00:14:29.740
You're insulting all the
hardworking tailors out there.

00:14:32.490 --> 00:14:35.700
So this is the cafe you're part of?

00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:38.500
Yeah, you can enjoy delicacies from all over the world.

00:14:39.210 --> 00:14:40.620
Try this.

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:42.130
That looks good.

00:14:42.580 --> 00:14:44.380
Here I go.

00:14:44.380 --> 00:14:47.050
Could I take a picture of you guys eating?

00:14:47.050 --> 00:14:48.380
Sure.

00:14:48.380 --> 00:14:50.470
Oh yeah, what meat is this?

00:14:50.470 --> 00:14:51.930
Bull penis.

00:14:53.180 --> 00:14:56.640
